{"id": "EUVD-2026-64566", "enisaUuid": "9c5c57f3-b54a-3f91-9634-b2630f8ca619", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet/dibs: Correct freeing of dmb_clientid_arr\n\nA dibs device interrupt handler can be active after dibs_dev_del() and\nmay still access dmb_clientid_arr. (UAF)\n\nIn case of a failure in dibs_dev_add() being called by dibs_lo_dev_probe()\ndmb_clientid_arr is freed twice (double free).\n\nFree dmb_clientid_arr in dibs_dev_release() after last reference is gone.\nNote that allocating in dibs_dev_add() instead of dibs_dev_alloc() is ok\nfor now, because no dmbs can be registered before dibs_dev_add().", "datePublished": "2026-08-22T15:32:10", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T19:06:03", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ece6426b61241e9bfb41aa131f235168f55229b1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7a1df20a8d2cc89e3a442b6e0b43b1cacde8d403", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9e6869be49064915edb6c8776b27c376cfdb0df5"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-74629", "GHSA-8jrf-fhpg-2ggp"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.38, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "384638a6-a284-32ed-8dc0-6ad9f9beaa7f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cc21191b584c6f7836b0f10774f8278b7cbfba10 <ece6426b61241e9bfb41aa131f235168f55229b1"}, {"id": "6fbb68f8-1a4b-3a44-993b-0e5019e3ed37", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.18"}, {"id": "7b0e0429-cae5-3f64-b7f1-d44b2fa62b1e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.9"}, {"id": "8674f87f-38dd-3b0c-813f-5bbbf7e2e8e4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cc21191b584c6f7836b0f10774f8278b7cbfba10 <7a1df20a8d2cc89e3a442b6e0b43b1cacde8d403"}, {"id": "8f6ce62e-7f08-38f8-a09d-f906366e2865", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor"